1
00:00:01,510 --> 00:00:03,550
Previously on "Final Space"...

2
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:05,070
Gary and Quinn go
on their first date

3
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:06,550
while the Earth is being
sucked up into the breach.

4
00:00:06,590 --> 00:00:07,900
Holy crap!

5
00:00:07,930 --> 00:00:09,730
Gary finds
the anti-matter bomb,

6
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:11,210
But to detonate it,
they're gonna have to get past

7
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:13,320
the Lord Commander's
fleet of incinerators.

8
00:00:13,350 --> 00:00:14,940
Can they save the world?

9
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:19,980
Get ready for the epic season
finale of "Final Space"!

10
00:00:23,470 --> 00:00:31,370
♪♪

11
00:00:31,410 --> 00:00:39,070
♪♪

12
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:41,590
Lord Commander:
Do these fools really think

13
00:00:41,620 --> 00:00:44,590
that I'll allow them
to close the breach?

14
00:00:44,630 --> 00:00:48,630
I was chosen by Titans.

15
00:00:48,660 --> 00:00:50,630
Gary: We might not
make it out of this.

16
00:00:50,670 --> 00:00:53,980
I wanted to say...
I don't know what we are.

17
00:00:54,010 --> 00:00:55,190
A crew?

18
00:00:55,220 --> 00:00:56,600
Feels like we're more than that.

19
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:58,360
I mean, friends maybe?

20
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:03,610
But to me, we've become like a
close, but very strange family.

21
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:06,960
And without you...
I wouldn't be me.

22
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:08,240
Us! Us! Us! Us!

23
00:01:08,270 --> 00:01:09,310
UU-U-U-Us!

24
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:10,760
Shut the hell up, KVN!

25
00:01:10,790 --> 00:01:13,100
I will never
leave you, Gary.

26
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:14,660
I will be your deep space

27
00:01:14,690 --> 00:01:17,560
insanity avoidance
forever companion.

28
00:01:17,590 --> 00:01:19,210
I swear to God, KVN!

29
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:22,460
Anyways, whatever happens,
wherever we go,

30
00:01:22,490 --> 00:01:25,800
we find each other
when this is over.

31
00:01:25,840 --> 00:01:27,080
Deal?

32
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:34,500
♪♪

33
00:01:34,540 --> 00:01:42,240
♪♪

34
00:01:42,270 --> 00:01:49,930
♪♪

35
00:01:49,970 --> 00:01:57,700
♪♪

36
00:02:01,910 --> 00:02:05,150
♪♪

37
00:02:05,190 --> 00:02:06,600
There are too many, Gary.

38
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:07,980
We'll never be able
to break through.

39
00:02:08,020 --> 00:02:09,500
H.U.E.,
can't you find a way?

40
00:02:09,540 --> 00:02:12,060
We can create
a Level 4 Particle Burn.

41
00:02:12,090 --> 00:02:14,160
Great. While I bust out
my chemistry set,

42
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:15,890
how about explaining
what the hell that means?!

43
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:18,890
It means we eject
our lightfold core...

44
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:20,380
and detonate it.What?!

45
00:02:20,410 --> 00:02:23,310
Your great idea is to explode
our lightfold engine?!

46
00:02:23,350 --> 00:02:25,110
Ooo-whoa.

47
00:02:28,110 --> 00:02:29,280
H.U.E., eject the --

48
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:30,700
[ Rattling ]

49
00:02:31,220 --> 00:02:32,220
Done, Gary.

50
00:02:32,250 --> 00:02:33,560
Seriously?

51
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:35,910
I mean, next time,
can you warn me first?

52
00:02:35,940 --> 00:02:37,320
Gary...

53
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:39,220
there is no "next time."

54
00:02:39,260 --> 00:02:41,360
♪♪

55
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:45,090
Detonating in 3...2...

56
00:02:45,130 --> 00:02:46,510
What is that?

57
00:02:46,540 --> 00:02:47,960
[ Electricity crackles ]...Boomtown.

58
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:54,200
[ Crashing ]

59
00:02:55,450 --> 00:02:58,210
[ Explosions, crashes continue ]

60
00:03:01,250 --> 00:03:03,590
[ Woosh ]

61
00:03:03,630 --> 00:03:05,730
H.U.E.,
full speed toward the breach.

62
00:03:05,770 --> 00:03:08,110
We got a freakin' hole
to close.

63
00:03:08,150 --> 00:03:19,120
♪♪

64
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:20,230
Is this fun?

65
00:03:20,260 --> 00:03:22,090
It is!
It is fun!

66
00:03:22,130 --> 00:03:25,270
♪♪

67
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:27,440
[ Echoing explosions ]

68
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:29,410
Release the hives.

69
00:03:29,450 --> 00:03:30,790
[ Retches ]

70
00:03:30,830 --> 00:03:33,280
[ Gasps ]
Crush them!

71
00:03:34,450 --> 00:03:37,280
[ Swarm buzzing ]

72
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:38,870
♪♪

73
00:03:38,900 --> 00:03:40,910
H.U.E.:
Shields up, Gary.

74
00:03:40,940 --> 00:03:42,150
H.U.E.,
what the crap is that?

75
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:44,700
The Lord Commander's
hive ships, Gary.

76
00:03:44,740 --> 00:03:46,050
If they eat through the shields,

77
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:48,080
there will be
nothing left to stop them.

78
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:49,640
How long will
the shields hold?

79
00:03:49,670 --> 00:03:52,810
Shield Integrity
is at 79% and dropping.

80
00:03:52,850 --> 00:03:55,400
That's like a --
That's like a B-minus!

81
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:57,130
We're still good!

82
00:03:57,990 --> 00:03:59,890
[ Beeping ]Now at 63%.

83
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:02,790
Oh, crap! That's,
like, a D, at best!

84
00:04:02,820 --> 00:04:05,140
KVN, if you don't get
on the outside turret,

85
00:04:05,170 --> 00:04:07,280
I will beat you within
one inch of your life.

86
00:04:07,310 --> 00:04:10,620
Guys, I'm the most expendable!
Congratulations to me.

87
00:04:10,660 --> 00:04:12,320
Mooncake,
what are you doing?

88
00:04:12,350 --> 00:04:14,280
Chookity pok.

89
00:04:14,320 --> 00:04:15,840
[ Sighs ]

90
00:04:15,870 --> 00:04:18,700
All right.
But you're not expendable.

91
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:22,910
[ Buzzing ]

92
00:04:22,950 --> 00:04:25,160
H.U.E.: Gary, the hives
have breached the shield.

93
00:04:25,190 --> 00:04:28,820
KVN and Mooncake won't be able
to hold them off for long.

94
00:04:28,850 --> 00:04:30,750
The odds of getting
to the bomb to the breach

95
00:04:30,780 --> 00:04:32,750
are now nearly impossible.

96
00:04:32,780 --> 00:04:34,130
S.A.M.E.S.:
Oh, no! Oh, no!

97
00:04:34,170 --> 00:04:36,930
This isn't a fight.
It's a death sentence.

98
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:38,310
Can a Hawk punch
through the hive?

99
00:04:38,340 --> 00:04:40,860
H.U.E.: Provided there
is sufficient force, yes.

100
00:04:40,900 --> 00:04:42,210
Then we will
load the anti-matter bomb

101
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:43,860
onto a Hawk and use that.

102
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:46,110
But as soon as the
drones see the Hawk,
they'll destroy it.

103
00:04:46,140 --> 00:04:48,660
Not if we send somebody
out first to clear the way.

104
00:04:50,180 --> 00:04:51,360
I'll do it.

105
00:04:51,390 --> 00:04:52,870
This is no job for a kid.

106
00:04:52,910 --> 00:04:55,980
I don't see a kid anymore.
I see a Man-Cat.

107
00:04:56,010 --> 00:04:58,120
Quinn, I can do this.

108
00:04:58,150 --> 00:04:59,950
We will go
with Little Cato.

109
00:04:59,980 --> 00:05:01,710
So that he doesn't
die like his father.

110
00:05:01,740 --> 00:05:03,230
Whoops, that was
insensitive.

111
00:05:03,260 --> 00:05:04,400
Sorry.

112
00:05:06,270 --> 00:05:08,540
Make us proud.

113
00:05:08,580 --> 00:05:09,960
H.U.E., get him a Hawk.

114
00:05:09,990 --> 00:05:12,000
Be careful out there,
Man-Cat.

115
00:05:12,030 --> 00:05:14,170
Don't worry. I got this.

116
00:05:14,210 --> 00:05:15,660
I so got this.

117
00:05:15,690 --> 00:05:17,660
[ Fading ]
I got this so good.

118
00:05:17,690 --> 00:05:20,070
Oooh, I got it.
I'm gonna get this...

119
00:05:20,110 --> 00:05:22,420
[ Buzzing ]

120
00:05:23,660 --> 00:05:24,660
[ Shoop ]

121
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:27,010
[ Electrical whirring ]

122
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:30,950
All right,
it's ready to go.

123
00:05:32,430 --> 00:05:33,710
[ Woosh ]

124
00:05:35,780 --> 00:05:38,370
To think, that's the only
thing stopping the Earth

125
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:39,750
from getting swallowed up.

126
00:05:39,780 --> 00:05:41,340
And it's all on me.

127
00:05:41,370 --> 00:05:43,200
I thought it would've
looked much cooler.

128
00:05:43,230 --> 00:05:44,750
Should I draw
some flames on it?

129
00:05:44,790 --> 00:05:46,580
I brought various tubes
of this.

130
00:05:46,620 --> 00:05:48,410
No! How about you don't
draw flames

131
00:05:48,450 --> 00:05:49,520
on the anti-matter bomb?!

132
00:05:49,550 --> 00:05:51,100
Is it too late?

133
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:53,140
[ Whispering ]
It is.

134
00:05:55,250 --> 00:05:58,350
-What if I can't do it?
-Try your best.

135
00:05:58,390 --> 00:06:00,940
What if my best
isn't good enough?

136
00:06:00,980 --> 00:06:02,390
It's good enough for me.

137
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:05,770
Have I made things
better?

138
00:06:05,810 --> 00:06:07,360
I did!

139
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:08,880
It's go time.

140
00:06:10,300 --> 00:06:12,440
-What are you doing?
-Finishing the job.

141
00:06:12,470 --> 00:06:14,750
Except I'm the one
taking it to the breach.

142
00:06:14,780 --> 00:06:16,790
It's my mission.
-Too bad.

143
00:06:16,820 --> 00:06:19,060
It's my destiny.

144
00:06:21,820 --> 00:06:23,210
Why are you fighting me?

145
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:26,210
Because I can take anything,
except losing you!

146
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:30,250
Oh, God, why, Quinn?!
Why are we in this situation?!

147
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:33,110
From the moment I discovered
the gravitational disturbance,

148
00:06:33,150 --> 00:06:35,150
I knew this
was my life's work.

149
00:06:35,180 --> 00:06:38,150
If you really have
feelings for me...

150
00:06:38,190 --> 00:06:40,120
let me see this
through to the end.

151
00:06:40,150 --> 00:06:42,430
I am genuinely
perplexed here!

152
00:06:42,470 --> 00:06:44,160
[ Ship rumbles ]

153
00:06:44,190 --> 00:06:47,540
'Cause I'm -- I'm trying
to stop you from dying.

154
00:06:47,570 --> 00:06:49,300
Please.

155
00:06:50,850 --> 00:06:52,300
Then, Quinn Ergon,

156
00:06:52,340 --> 00:06:56,720
I will use every last breath
to make sure you succeed.

157
00:06:56,760 --> 00:06:59,340
That's a real, raw promise.

158
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,970
Hwa!
Mmm.

159
00:07:03,490 --> 00:07:04,730
Hell...
Hell, yeah!

160
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:06,420
More of that
when you come back.

161
00:07:06,460 --> 00:07:07,490
Don't die on me.

162
00:07:07,530 --> 00:07:10,290
Funny, I thought
I was gonna be the hero...

163
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:11,910
but it's you.

164
00:07:11,940 --> 00:07:14,740
No, it's both of us.

165
00:07:14,770 --> 00:07:17,360
Always has been.

166
00:07:20,640 --> 00:07:22,580
[ Hive buzzing ]

167
00:07:22,610 --> 00:07:24,020
[ Buttons click, beep ]

168
00:07:24,060 --> 00:07:25,540
[ Thrusters humming ]

169
00:07:27,410 --> 00:07:29,550
Punch a hole for me, boys!

170
00:07:34,410 --> 00:07:37,560
Okay, guys,
all together now.

171
00:07:43,390 --> 00:07:45,870
-Thanks, Little Cato.
-Finish it, Quinn.

172
00:07:45,910 --> 00:07:49,950
♪♪

173
00:07:49,980 --> 00:07:51,980
If only there was
more help to call on.

174
00:07:52,020 --> 00:07:53,780
If only there was a resistance.

175
00:07:53,810 --> 00:07:57,710
Wait, there is a resistance,
and I'm its leader.

176
00:07:57,750 --> 00:08:00,650
Resistance?
Is it time to resist? It is!

177
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:03,340
This is
General Tribore Menendez.

178
00:08:03,370 --> 00:08:05,720
All battalions to Sector 11.

179
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:07,170
Reeeeorr!

180
00:08:07,210 --> 00:08:08,620
Reeeeorr!

181
00:08:08,660 --> 00:08:09,730
Reeeeorr!

182
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:11,070
Reeeeorr!

183
00:08:11,110 --> 00:08:12,560
Reeeeorr!

184
00:08:12,590 --> 00:08:15,520
H.U.E.: The hives have
infiltrated the Galaxy One.

185
00:08:16,700 --> 00:08:18,080
Hey!

186
00:08:18,110 --> 00:08:19,910
Get off my ship!

187
00:08:19,940 --> 00:08:22,320
Aaahhhh!

188
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:25,120
[ Drones buzzing, splattering ]

189
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:31,370
[ Explosion ]

190
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:35,130
[ Explosion ]

191
00:08:37,410 --> 00:08:40,100
Is this what death
feels like? [ Whirs ]

192
00:08:40,140 --> 00:08:42,760
Not bad.
It's just weird.

193
00:08:42,790 --> 00:08:44,100
Closing in.

194
00:08:45,310 --> 00:08:48,210
Ah! Am I alone here?

195
00:08:48,250 --> 00:08:50,730
No. Tribore's here.

196
00:08:50,770 --> 00:08:54,670
And I brought some
special friends.

197
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:56,220
Ahh!

198
00:08:57,910 --> 00:08:59,260
Thanks, Tribore.

199
00:08:59,290 --> 00:09:01,540
I'm closing in
on the breach.

200
00:09:05,330 --> 00:09:08,270
Is this bad?
It sure the hell is!

201
00:09:09,230 --> 00:09:12,410
No, Tribore.
I loved you.

202
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:13,960
Who's leading
the resistance now?

203
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,690
I am. First order
of business --

204
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:18,590
revenge.

205
00:09:18,620 --> 00:09:20,870
♪♪

206
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:22,320
Eject!

207
00:09:27,350 --> 00:09:29,360
[ Pipes clank ]

208
00:09:30,910 --> 00:09:32,570
[ Gun cocks ]

209
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:35,810
KVN: Yes.
Two at once! Nice shot.

210
00:09:35,850 --> 00:09:38,950
Down you go!
Gotcha! Gotcha! Gotcha.

211
00:09:38,990 --> 00:09:40,230
[ Drones buzzing ]

212
00:09:40,260 --> 00:09:41,850
Wow!
I'm impressed with myself.

213
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:45,750
[ Gasps ]
Ooh.

214
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:49,000
Hey, Gary?
-What is it, KVN?!

215
00:09:49,030 --> 00:09:50,620
[ Electricity crackles ]

216
00:09:50,650 --> 00:09:53,170
-It's been fun, right?
-Oh! KVN!

217
00:09:53,210 --> 00:09:54,930
I guess? Hey!

218
00:09:54,970 --> 00:09:56,690
[ Breaking down ]
I had fun...

219
00:09:58,700 --> 00:10:00,770
It's so beautiful.

220
00:10:02,980 --> 00:10:07,840
Call back the hives and
ready the dimension splitter.

221
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:11,540
[ Muffled Lasers, explosions ]

222
00:10:11,570 --> 00:10:14,510
♪♪

223
00:10:14,540 --> 00:10:15,580
Chookity!

224
00:10:17,470 --> 00:10:19,230
[ Electrical hum ]Ooh...

225
00:10:20,990 --> 00:10:22,440
Mooncake!

226
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:23,310
No!

227
00:10:23,340 --> 00:10:24,830
[ Shink! ]Ah!

228
00:10:24,860 --> 00:10:27,620
Uh!

229
00:10:27,660 --> 00:10:29,930
[ Moaning ]

230
00:10:29,970 --> 00:10:31,040
[ Drones buzzing ]

231
00:10:31,070 --> 00:10:32,590
Ohhh...

232
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:36,220
Chookity pok!

233
00:10:36,250 --> 00:10:37,700
[ Electricity crackles ]

234
00:10:37,740 --> 00:10:43,050
The more you resist,
the stronger the trap becomes.

235
00:10:43,090 --> 00:10:45,710
Lord Commander:
[ Maniacally ] Hey, Mooncake...

236
00:10:45,740 --> 00:10:50,710
We're going to have
a lot of fun.

237
00:10:50,750 --> 00:10:55,030
A.I.: Approaching breach.Here goes everything.

238
00:10:55,060 --> 00:10:56,750
[ Ship rattling ]

239
00:10:57,760 --> 00:10:59,240
[ Electricity crackling,
alarms beeping ]

240
00:10:59,270 --> 00:11:01,860
[ Explosion ]

241
00:11:01,900 --> 00:11:03,690
[ Quinn groans ]

242
00:11:03,730 --> 00:11:04,970
Ugh![ Beeps ]

243
00:11:08,010 --> 00:11:11,420
[ Wooshing ]Aaah!

244
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:15,980
♪♪

245
00:11:16,020 --> 00:11:19,230
[ Siren blaring ]

246
00:11:19,260 --> 00:11:22,230
[ Gary groaning ]

247
00:11:22,260 --> 00:11:23,090
[ Siren stops ]

248
00:11:23,130 --> 00:11:25,610
[ Grunts ]

249
00:11:25,650 --> 00:11:26,990
Ugh...

250
00:11:27,030 --> 00:11:28,960
Agh!

251
00:11:30,310 --> 00:11:31,760
Ughh!

252
00:11:31,790 --> 00:11:32,860
[ Metallic clink ]

253
00:11:32,890 --> 00:11:35,760
[ Groans ]
Status report.

254
00:11:35,790 --> 00:11:37,350
[ Electrical hum ]

255
00:11:37,380 --> 00:11:40,450
H.U.E.: Gary, we have lost
the Galaxy One.

256
00:11:40,490 --> 00:11:41,940
We still have
a left pulse engine.

257
00:11:41,970 --> 00:11:43,730
It is the right
pulse engine,

258
00:11:43,770 --> 00:11:47,010
and it is not enough
to face the Lord Commander.

259
00:11:47,050 --> 00:11:50,460
Gary, there's one option
you haven't considered.

260
00:11:50,500 --> 00:11:52,470
You can abandon ship.

261
00:11:52,500 --> 00:11:54,880
I'm not running away.
Not this time.

262
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:56,920
At one point,
that made sense, but...

263
00:11:56,950 --> 00:11:58,710
I'm not
that guy anymore.

264
00:11:58,750 --> 00:12:00,300
I'd give you a cookie.

265
00:12:00,340 --> 00:12:02,200
But I think you've
outgrown that now.

266
00:12:02,230 --> 00:12:03,270
What?!

267
00:12:03,300 --> 00:12:04,860
No! Give me a cookie!

268
00:12:04,890 --> 00:12:06,790
I will never, ever
outgrow a cookie!

269
00:12:06,820 --> 00:12:09,100
I'm sorry, Gary,
but they're gone.

270
00:12:09,140 --> 00:12:10,760
All gone.

271
00:12:10,790 --> 00:12:12,310
That sucks, H.U.E.!

272
00:12:12,350 --> 00:12:14,560
It...really does, Gary.

273
00:12:14,590 --> 00:12:16,560
We can't let
this guy win.

274
00:12:16,590 --> 00:12:18,490
Gary, I know that look.

275
00:12:18,530 --> 00:12:20,560
Reconsider. Please.

276
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:24,290
No way, José.
I won't reconsider.

277
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:25,980
[ Beep ]
[ Siren resumes ]

278
00:12:26,020 --> 00:12:29,160
Gary, you have set a collision
course directly for

279
00:12:29,190 --> 00:12:31,570
the Lord Commander's
Heavy Incinerator.

280
00:12:31,610 --> 00:12:32,990
[ Groans ]

281
00:12:33,020 --> 00:12:35,340
It's the only the way to stop
him from taking out Quinn.

282
00:12:35,370 --> 00:12:36,790
And I have to save Mooncake.

283
00:12:36,820 --> 00:12:39,790
Do I really have to make
a list for you right now?!

284
00:12:39,820 --> 00:12:42,520
If we're going out,
we're going out big.

285
00:12:42,550 --> 00:12:43,760
Agreed.

286
00:12:43,790 --> 00:12:45,170
We must do
everything possible

287
00:12:45,210 --> 00:12:46,970
to destroy
that dick loaf.

288
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:49,940
What do you say
we make an entrance?

289
00:12:49,970 --> 00:12:52,320
Right pulse engine
is a go.

290
00:12:52,350 --> 00:12:53,770
[ Engine humming faintly ]

291
00:12:55,740 --> 00:12:57,010
What?

292
00:12:57,050 --> 00:12:59,460
What is he trying to
accomplish?! [ Retches ]

293
00:12:59,500 --> 00:13:01,360
He's already lost everything.

294
00:13:01,400 --> 00:13:03,360
[ Rattling ]

295
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:07,090
Computer: Proximity alert!
Proximity alert!

296
00:13:07,130 --> 00:13:07,920
Fire!

297
00:13:07,950 --> 00:13:11,160
Rip that ship from space!

298
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:12,720
[ Alarm blaring ]

299
00:13:12,750 --> 00:13:19,660
♪♪

300
00:13:19,690 --> 00:13:26,630
♪♪

301
00:13:26,660 --> 00:13:33,570
♪♪

302
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:36,710
[ Lasers ricocheting ]

303
00:13:38,260 --> 00:13:39,400
Uhh!
[Thud]

304
00:13:39,430 --> 00:13:43,230
I wish killing you
could last a lifetime.

305
00:13:43,270 --> 00:13:45,410
♪♪

306
00:13:45,440 --> 00:13:46,650
Ready for your turn?

307
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:49,240
Get on with it!

308
00:13:49,270 --> 00:13:53,310
Aaaah!

309
00:13:53,340 --> 00:14:01,180
♪♪

310
00:14:01,210 --> 00:14:08,880
♪♪

311
00:14:08,910 --> 00:14:14,260
H.U.E.: [ Echoing, muffled ]
Gary, the Galaxy One...

312
00:14:14,300 --> 00:14:16,920
is destroyed...

313
00:14:16,950 --> 00:14:19,540
H.U.E., quick!
Transfer your AI into my helmet.

314
00:14:19,580 --> 00:14:21,030
No, no, no. H.U.E.!

315
00:14:21,060 --> 00:14:22,130
H.U.E.?!

316
00:14:23,130 --> 00:14:24,890
H.U.E.!

317
00:14:24,930 --> 00:14:26,170
H.U.E.:
Yes, Gary. I'm here.

318
00:14:26,210 --> 00:14:28,760
Oh, my gosh.
Don't ever leave me, H.U.E.

319
00:14:28,790 --> 00:14:30,620
Wouldn't think of it, Gary.
-Chookity!

320
00:14:30,660 --> 00:14:34,830
[ Mooncake whimpering ]

321
00:14:41,770 --> 00:14:43,390
[ Gary grunts ]

322
00:14:43,430 --> 00:14:47,090
Computer:
Final Space Dimension Splitter
has been armed.

323
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:50,300
15 seconds until activation.[ Retching ]

324
00:14:51,470 --> 00:14:53,650
[ Mooncake whimpering ]

325
00:14:53,680 --> 00:14:54,720
Mooncake!

326
00:14:54,750 --> 00:14:56,890
Here he is...

327
00:14:56,930 --> 00:14:59,930
the infamous hero!

328
00:14:59,960 --> 00:15:01,590
The Gary!

329
00:15:01,620 --> 00:15:03,730
Just Gary!

330
00:15:03,760 --> 00:15:06,380
Yes -- [heaves] --
just The Gary.

331
00:15:06,420 --> 00:15:09,040
Let him go!
He's done nothing to you!

332
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:12,600
You're just in time
to see Mooncake...

333
00:15:12,630 --> 00:15:17,390
[ Electricity crackles ]...open the doorway
of Final Space.

334
00:15:17,430 --> 00:15:18,500
[ Whimpering ]

335
00:15:18,530 --> 00:15:21,330
Hang tight, little buddy!

336
00:15:21,360 --> 00:15:22,810
[ Groans ]

337
00:15:22,850 --> 00:15:26,580
[ Howling ]

338
00:15:26,610 --> 00:15:30,860
[ Electricity crackling ]

339
00:15:30,890 --> 00:15:33,000
[ Distressed ]
Chookity!

340
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:35,900
[ Woosh ]

341
00:15:37,380 --> 00:15:39,620
Ugh!

342
00:15:39,660 --> 00:15:43,800
[ Echoing ] Can't you see?
There is no one beside you.

343
00:15:43,830 --> 00:15:47,180
Avocato, his son,
your crew?

344
00:15:47,220 --> 00:15:50,880
Everyone you've
cared about is gone!

345
00:15:50,910 --> 00:15:52,980
All because of that!

346
00:15:53,020 --> 00:15:56,090
And now, yourlife ends.

347
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:58,090
But nothing quick.

348
00:15:58,120 --> 00:15:59,850
I want you to experience

349
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:03,130
the same pain
you put me through.

350
00:16:03,160 --> 00:16:06,370
A slow, painful death.[ Rumbling woosh ]

351
00:16:06,410 --> 00:16:09,170
[ Straining ]
You don't get it, do you?

352
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:12,690
The good guys
win in the end!

353
00:16:12,730 --> 00:16:13,730
They always do.

354
00:16:13,760 --> 00:16:14,900
No.

355
00:16:14,930 --> 00:16:17,520
Not this time, The Gary.

356
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:19,150
Don't do this, Jack.

357
00:16:19,180 --> 00:16:21,220
Why would you
call me that?

358
00:16:21,250 --> 00:16:22,530
[ Frenzied ]
Speak!

359
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:23,910
You used to like taquitos

360
00:16:23,940 --> 00:16:26,150
and hanging out
with my dad, man.

361
00:16:26,190 --> 00:16:28,120
Ahh.

362
00:16:28,150 --> 00:16:30,920
John Goodspeed's son.

363
00:16:30,950 --> 00:16:33,850
Well...that changes nothing!

364
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:35,990
You don't need
to do this, Jack.

365
00:16:36,020 --> 00:16:37,920
Stop calling me that!

366
00:16:37,960 --> 00:16:41,930
That person died
the day I was chosen.

367
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:44,030
Can I be honest,
with the likelihood

368
00:16:44,070 --> 00:16:46,030
of pissing you off
a little bit?

369
00:16:46,070 --> 00:16:47,660
I don't think
you were chosen.

370
00:16:47,690 --> 00:16:51,250
You getting these powers
was just a mistake.

371
00:16:51,280 --> 00:16:52,700
Mistake?!

372
00:16:52,730 --> 00:16:56,940
Rraaaaahh!Aaahh!

373
00:16:56,980 --> 00:17:02,090
♪♪

374
00:17:02,120 --> 00:17:06,950
Now, let's take a look
at what's inside Final Space.

375
00:17:06,990 --> 00:17:09,060
[ Mooncake whimpering ]

376
00:17:09,090 --> 00:17:11,920
[ Shrieks ]

377
00:17:16,750 --> 00:17:18,860
[ Quinn groaning ]

378
00:17:18,890 --> 00:17:20,450
[ Gasps ]

379
00:17:20,480 --> 00:17:21,970
[ Straining ]

380
00:17:24,310 --> 00:17:25,630
[ Gasps ]

381
00:17:25,660 --> 00:17:27,460
Aaah!

382
00:17:27,490 --> 00:17:30,800
Lord Commander:
The time has come!

383
00:17:30,840 --> 00:17:31,910
Yes!

384
00:17:31,940 --> 00:17:33,390
[ Ominous snarl ]

385
00:17:34,740 --> 00:17:36,600
Take me!

386
00:17:37,840 --> 00:17:40,120
I'm ready to be a Titan

387
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:45,090
and rule every dimension!

388
00:17:46,090 --> 00:17:47,580
No! No!

389
00:17:47,610 --> 00:17:50,820
Nooo!

390
00:17:50,860 --> 00:17:52,930
[ Smashing ]

391
00:17:52,960 --> 00:18:02,280
♪♪

392
00:18:02,320 --> 00:18:04,290
[ Beep ]Quinn: Gary?

393
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:05,110
Quinn.

394
00:18:05,150 --> 00:18:07,120
I'm sorry.

395
00:18:07,150 --> 00:18:08,770
For...what?

396
00:18:08,810 --> 00:18:10,460
Not telling you sooner.

397
00:18:10,500 --> 00:18:12,330
You can tell me
when you come back.

398
00:18:12,360 --> 00:18:13,640
Gary...

399
00:18:13,670 --> 00:18:15,680
No, don't...

400
00:18:15,710 --> 00:18:18,020
Don't say it.

401
00:18:18,060 --> 00:18:20,060
I'm not coming back.

402
00:18:22,340 --> 00:18:23,370
Quinn.

403
00:18:24,370 --> 00:18:27,140
We've lost the Earth,
but I can still save you.

404
00:18:27,170 --> 00:18:29,550
Goodbye, Gary.

405
00:18:32,550 --> 00:18:34,280
I'll miss you.

406
00:18:35,830 --> 00:18:39,080
[ Rumbling ]

407
00:18:41,810 --> 00:18:43,190
Quinn?!

408
00:18:47,290 --> 00:18:49,540
You have got to be kidding.

409
00:18:49,570 --> 00:18:51,260
[ Retches ]

410
00:18:51,300 --> 00:18:54,160
[ Mooncake whimpers ]

411
00:18:54,200 --> 00:18:57,060
H.U.E., get her back.
Co-Come on.

412
00:18:57,100 --> 00:18:58,890
Quinn!

413
00:18:58,930 --> 00:19:00,310
H.U.E., get her back!

414
00:19:02,690 --> 00:19:04,210
Quinn!

415
00:19:07,380 --> 00:19:15,980
♪♪

416
00:19:16,010 --> 00:19:18,840
Gary:
H.U.E., what are my chances
of getting out of this mess?

417
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:20,080
H.U.E.:
In your current state,

418
00:19:20,120 --> 00:19:21,980
you will pass
the point of recovery

419
00:19:22,020 --> 00:19:24,470
in 10 minutes...

420
00:19:24,500 --> 00:19:25,810
9 minutes...

421
00:19:25,850 --> 00:19:27,200
8...

422
00:19:27,230 --> 00:19:28,060
7...

423
00:19:28,090 --> 00:19:29,650
Look, it's Carl.

424
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:31,540
6...It can't be...

425
00:19:31,580 --> 00:19:32,580
5...

426
00:19:32,610 --> 00:19:34,170
4...

427
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:35,550
3...

428
00:19:35,580 --> 00:19:36,930
2...

429
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:40,550
The cookies will be
done in one minute.

430
00:19:40,590 --> 00:19:42,110
[ Faintly ]
Oh, good.

431
00:19:42,140 --> 00:19:44,700
I'm extremely excited...

432
00:19:44,730 --> 00:19:46,210
for these cookies.

433
00:19:46,250 --> 00:19:47,730
Zero.

434
00:19:47,770 --> 00:19:50,530
Gary, the cookies are done.

435
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:54,600
[ Gasps faintly ]

436
00:19:56,400 --> 00:19:59,090
♪♪

437
00:19:59,120 --> 00:20:01,260
I'll miss you, friend.

438
00:20:01,300 --> 00:20:08,270
♪♪

439
00:20:08,310 --> 00:20:15,350
♪♪

440
00:20:15,380 --> 00:20:16,800
Hey, son.

441
00:20:16,830 --> 00:20:18,420
Holy crap.

442
00:20:18,450 --> 00:20:19,630
Am I dreaming?

443
00:20:19,660 --> 00:20:20,700
No.
Oh.

444
00:20:20,730 --> 00:20:23,250
Well.
Then...I'm...

445
00:20:23,290 --> 00:20:24,360
Yep.

446
00:20:24,390 --> 00:20:26,050
Well, crap,
that's not good.

447
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:28,080
You see, I was --
I was hoping for a no.

448
00:20:28,120 --> 00:20:30,220
I was sent to give you
a choice --

449
00:20:30,260 --> 00:20:32,470
to come with me
or to go back.

450
00:20:32,500 --> 00:20:34,540
What's...that way?

451
00:20:34,570 --> 00:20:37,270
Lots, and I mean
lots, of imported beer.

452
00:20:37,300 --> 00:20:40,890
It's actually ridiculous.How much beer are we talking?

453
00:20:40,920 --> 00:20:42,650
Too much.

454
00:20:42,680 --> 00:20:44,270
And back that way?

455
00:20:44,310 --> 00:20:47,170
A perilous journey full
of death and heartbreak.

456
00:20:47,340 --> 00:20:51,620
Which way
is Little Cato?

457
00:20:51,660 --> 00:20:54,830
Which way is Mooncake?

458
00:20:54,870 --> 00:20:57,290
Which way is Quinn?

459
00:20:57,320 --> 00:21:04,670
♪♪

460
00:21:04,710 --> 00:21:12,300
♪♪

461
00:21:12,340 --> 00:21:19,650
♪♪

462
00:21:19,690 --> 00:21:27,040
♪♪

463
00:21:27,070 --> 00:21:34,910
♪♪
